{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774127828,"nonce":"33xQeRXj8/uHL3RwwhyBj9I+9ww=","title":"Consider moving agent-commit, wt, mandible CLI from dotfiles into mandible/cli/","message":"agent-commit, wt/dwt/wt-merge/wt-sync, and the mandible CLI wrapper currently live in ~/.dotfiles/bin/. These are Mandible operational tools — they call Mandible APIs, manage Mandible-specific workflows, and are tightly coupled to Mandible conventions.\n\nFor Mandible to be distributable (Tauri Level 2, fdc0e8a), it should ship its own tooling. Moving these to mandible/cli/ would:\n- Make version coupling explicit (scripts and daemon in the same repo)\n- Eliminate the dotfiles dependency for new users\n- Enable the Tauri app to bundle them as sidecar binaries\n\nDotfiles would then just add mandible/cli/ to PATH (or symlink).\n\nThis is a distribution/packaging concern, not urgent, but should be resolved before release.","files":null}]}